content:
A processor is supposed to run a strictly one-way data flow: operations arrive through `onOperations`, and any resulting mutation leaves through `dispatch`. The `dispatch` object is handed to the factory on `IProcessorHostModule`, and its only method is `execute`:

```typescript
interface IProcessorDispatch {
  execute(
    docId: string,
    branch: string,
    actions: Action[],
    signal?: AbortSignal,
    meta?: Record<string, unknown>,
  ): Promise<ProcessorDispatchResult>;
}

type ProcessorDispatchResult = {
  id: string;      // job ID
  status: string;  // job status at time of submission
};
```

Under the hood `dispatch.execute()` calls `reactorClient.executeAsync()`. The returned `status` is the status *at submission*, so awaiting the promise tells you the job was accepted, never that it landed. The canonical shape is a processor that watches for a state transition and fires an action at a different document:

```typescript
if (operation.action.type === "SET_STATUS" &&
    operation.action.input?.status === "approved") {
  await this.dispatch.execute(this.paymentDocId, "main", [
    { type: "CREATE_PAYMENT",
      input: { invoiceId: context.documentId, amount: operation.action.input.amount },
      scope: "global" },
  ]);
}
```

The processor dispatches and moves on. If it needs to observe the result, the correct move is to widen its own `ProcessorFilter` to include the target document type so the resulting operations come back through a later `onOperations` call — not to await the outcome. That constraint is what keeps a processor from waiting on work that depends on the processor itself finishing.

Because backfill and restart-gap replay can re-deliver the same operations, a dispatching processor also wants an idempotence guard: check the target document's state (or a dedup key in it) before dispatching, so a replayed batch does not double-fire the side action.

Provenance: academy `03-Build/04-WorkWithData/05-ProcessorBestPractices.md` (published), confirmed against `packages/shared/processors/types.ts` and `apps/connect/src/store/processor-host-module.ts` at monorepo 6.2.2-dev.45.
